1.  Calculate the volume of the pool in cubic feet. \begin{align*}  \text{Volume} &= \text{length} \times \text{width} \times \text{depth} \\ &= 25 \text{ feet} \times 14 \text{ feet} \times 4 \text{ feet} \\ &= 1400 \text{ cubic feet} \end{align*}
2.  Multiply the volume by 5.9 to find the number of gallons needed. \begin{align*} \text{Gallons} &= \text{Volume} \times 5.9 \\ &= 1400 \text{ cubic feet} \times 5.9 \\ &= 8260 \text{ gallons} \end{align*}
3.  Calculate the cost to fill the pool by multiplying the number of gallons needed by the cost per gallon. \begin{align*} \text{Cost} &= \text{Gallons} \times \text{Cost per gallon} \\ &= 8260 \text{ gallons} \times $0.10 \text{ per gallon} \\ &= $826 \end{align*}
Therefore, it will cost $826 to fill the pool.

\boxed{826}

