60% more than normal means we have to add 60% of the normal cost to the normal cost. First, calculate 60% of $120: 0.60 * $120 = $72. Then, add this amount to the normal cost: $120 + $72 = $192. James pays $192 a month. To find the yearly cost, we multiply the monthly cost by 12: $192 * 12 = $2304.
So, James pays $2304 a year.

\boxed{2304}
